      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RPC requests sent by module",
      "description": "Requests per second the core publishes to the RPC request topic for each module (1-minute rate). This is the offered load on the Kafka RPC path. During a pm-snmp benchmark the snmp and collect modules dominate; the other modules should be near zero. A module flat-lining at a round number usually means a scheduler, not Kafka, is the bottleneck.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
