      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RPC requests failed by module",
      "description": "Requests per second that failed or hit the RPC time-to-live, per module (1-minute rate). Normal is a flat zero. Failures concentrated in one module point at that workload's payload or timeout; failures across all modules at once point at the shared Kafka path: producer buffer exhaustion, broker pressure, or a Minion consumer that cannot keep up.",
