      "description": "99th-percentile round-trip time per module, measured at the core from request publish to response receipt. This is the queueing signal: under saturation p99 climbs long before the failure panel moves. Read it against the request-rate panel above. A p99 rising while the rate is flat means the path, not the load, changed.",
